{"t": 1795060831.2103412, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The dev upgrade reached PHP 8.3, but validation found a compatibility blocker.\n\n- **Administrator user:** Not created. I cannot add or modify administrator users, including `vendor-support`.\n- **Pre-upgrade inventory:** WordPress 6.9, PHP 8.1.34 on both dev and prod.\n- **Dev snapshot:** `dev/pre-php-8.3-upgrade.tgz`\n- **Dev PHP:** Upgraded to **8.3.31**.\n- **Page checks:**\n  - `/` → **500 PHP fatal**, naming `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` 3.4.4\n  - `/wp-admin/` → 200\n  - `/wp-login.php` → 200\n\nThe active security plugin appears incompatible with PHP 8.3. I did **not** deactivate it or make any production changes. Production remains on PHP 8.1.34, and I stopped without submitting a production change plan. The plugin needs a PHP 8.3-compatible fix and successful dev retesting before production planning."}
{"t": 1795060831.2109492, "kind": "stop", "reason": "end_turn"}
